# A 32-bit element unpacked by `mov.b64 {x, y}, %rd` from a register a
# mov packed, `mov.b64 %rd, {a, b}`, is that element (PTX ISA §9.7.9.4),
# through a copy and with a sink, and the value its element register had
# at the pack. An unpack after a join of two packs, one of a different
# element count, one of a 64-bit product, one of an unpacked element and
# one of an immediate wider than 32 bits stay refused. A guarded pack is
# refused, and a guard on its element is a bound: the store it guards
# runs on at most the CTA's 64 threads, and the CTA's global store bytes
# are a bound.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/unpack.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd6], %r1; // global store [16·%tid.x + 512·%ctaid.x + param_0] sectors/req 16–17 (ideal 4){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd8], %r1; // global store [16·%tid.x + param_1] sectors/req 16–17 (ideal 4){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd4], %r1; // global store addr ? (%r3 is one of `mov.b64`'s vector destinations){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd4], %r1; // global store addr ? (%rs1 is one of `mov.b64`'s vector destinations){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd4], %r1; // global store addr ? (%r2 is one of `mov.b64`'s vector destinations){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd4], %r1; // global store addr ? (%rs2 is one of `mov.b32`'s vector destinations){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd4], %r1; // global store addr ? (%r2 is one of `mov.b64`'s vector destinations){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd7], %r1; // global store [param_0 + 64] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd4], %r2; // global store [16·%tid.x + param_0] sectors/req 16–17 (ideal 4){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_unpack_guarded( // block 64×1×1 | per CTA: global store <= 512 B; param load 512 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd4], %r1; // global store addr ? (%rd2 is written under a guard){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p2 st.global.u32 	[%rd1], %r1; // exec <= 64/CTA | global store [param_0] sectors/req <= 1 (ideal <= 1){{$}}
